# ServiceToolPoC architecture

Read `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` for full detail. Enforce these rules on every edit under `src/`.

## Layers (top → bottom)

- `features/*/screens|components` — Presentation (View): JSX/styles only
- `features/*/hooks` — Application (ViewModel): orchestrates domain + services
- `domain/` — pure business logic; no React or BLE imports
- `services/` — infrastructure (BLE, storage, permissions); no JSX

## Import rules

```typescript
// ❌ Screen importing BLE library
import { BleManager } from 'react-native-ble-plx';  // in features/*/screens/

// ❌ Domain importing React Native
import { Platform } from 'react-native';  // in domain/

// ❌ Cross-feature import
import { useBleClient } from '../../client/hooks/useBleClient';  // in features/tool/

// ✅ Screen uses its feature hook
import { useBleClient } from '../hooks/useBleClient';

// ✅ Hook uses service + domain
import { BleCentralService } from '../../../services/ble/BleCentralService';
import { parseTelemetryBase64 } from '../../../domain/telemetry/parse';
```

## Where new code goes

| Change | Location |
|--------|----------|
| New screen or UI widget | `features/<feature>/screens` or `components` |
| New screen state / BLE orchestration | `features/<feature>/hooks` |
| Parse, validate, policy, math | `domain/` |
| Library wrapper, scan, permissions | `services/` |
| Shared TS interfaces | `types/` |

## Hooks and screens

- Hooks expose `{ state, actions }`; screens stay thin (layout + call actions).
- No business logic in screens beyond display formatting.

## Tests

- `domain/` tests: no mocks.
- `services/` tests: mock native BLE modules.
- Mirror source paths under `__tests__/`.
